WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:19.605
next day the rain was still pouring down, and the moor was hidden in mist.

2
00:00:20.826 --> 00:00:22.987
It was not a good day for going outdoors.

3
00:00:24.268 --> 00:00:28.250
Mary had to wait until afternoon to talk to Martha, who was busy working.

4
00:00:29.431 --> 00:00:31.392
At last Martha came to Mary's room.

5
00:00:32.576 --> 00:00:35.859
The two girls sat by the fire, and Martha took out her knitting.

6
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.442
"I've found out what that crying was," Mary announced.

7
00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:43.725
Martha let her knitting fall on her lap.

8
00:00:44.285 --> 00:00:45.006
"You haven't!"

9
00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:47.448
"I heard it last night.

10
00:00:47.948 --> 00:00:50.970
When I got up to see where it was coming from, I met Colin."

11
00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.132
"Oh no!

12
00:00:53.793 --> 00:00:56.054
Everyone will think I told you where he is."

13
00:00:56.715 --> 00:00:57.836
Martha started to cry.

14
00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:03.233
"I'll lose my job here, and what will Mother do?

15
00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.633
We need my wages!"

16
00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:07.354
"You won't lose your job.

17
00:01:07.694 --> 00:01:08.794
We talked and talked.

18
00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.875
He showed me the picture of his mother, and I sang him to sleep.

19
00:01:13.355 --> 00:01:14.436
I think he liked me."

20
00:01:15.696 --> 00:01:17.077
Martha could not believe this.

21
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:22.018
Colin was a bad-tempered, spoiled boy who didn't like anyone.

22
00:01:23.278 --> 00:01:24.919
"You must have bewitched him!"

23
00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.479
Mary shook her head.

24
00:01:27.499 --> 00:01:31.185
"I heard about magic in India, but I can't make any.

25
00:01:32.406 --> 00:01:33.888
He seems to believe he's dying.

26
00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:36.510
Do you think he'll really die?"

27
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:42.956
"Mother says all children need fresh air," Martha stated, picking up her knitting again.

28
00:01:42.976 --> 00:01:49.121
"But all that boy does is lie in bed all day, looking at books and taking medicine."

29
00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:52.844
Mary stared at the fire.

30
00:01:52.865 --> 00:01:59.793
"I wonder," she said slowly, "if it would do him good to go out into a garden and

31
00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.994
watch things growing.

32
00:02:02.314 --> 00:02:03.375
I know it did me good."

33
00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:07.917
Before Martha could answer, a bell rang, and she stood up.

34
00:02:07.937 --> 00:02:11.999
"That's probably his nurse wanting me to sit with him."

35
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.381
Martha returned in a few minutes.

36
00:02:16.401 --> 00:02:19.322
"Well, you have bewitched him.

37
00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:23.124
He's sitting up on his sofa with his picture books.

38
00:02:24.428 --> 00:02:29.132
He told the nurse to stay away until six o'clock, and he wants you to come see him."

39
00:02:30.413 --> 00:02:32.255
Mary followed Martha to Colin's room.

40
00:02:33.896 --> 00:02:39.161
She was surprised that the room looked so beautiful in the daylight and that Colin looked less pale.

41
00:02:39.181 --> 00:02:42.924
"Come here," he said after Martha left.

42
00:02:42.944 --> 00:02:45.486
"I've been thinking of you today."

43
00:02:45.506 --> 00:02:47.928
"I've been thinking of you too."

44
00:02:49.149 --> 00:02:52.632
Mary told him how afraid Martha was that she would lose her job.

45
00:02:54.188 --> 00:02:55.129
"Tell her to come here."

46
00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.353
Mary went into the next room and brought back a very frightened Martha.

47
00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:04.956
"Must everyone in this house do as I please?"

48
00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:06.817
Colin asked her sternly.

49
00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:09.719
"Yes, sir," said Martha.

50
00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:15.243
"Then if I order you to bring Mary to me, no one can send you away."

51
00:03:15.263 --> 00:03:17.024
"No, sir.

52
00:03:17.484 --> 00:03:19.306
I just want to do my duty, sir."

53
00:03:19.326 --> 00:03:22.168
"I want you to do your duty too.

54
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.421
I'll take care of you.

55
00:03:24.741 --> 00:03:25.542
Now go away."

56
00:03:26.903 --> 00:03:28.645
Martha curtsied and left the room.

57
00:03:28.665 --> 00:03:31.947
"Why are you looking at me like that?"

58
00:03:32.368 --> 00:03:33.589
Colin demanded of Mary.

59
00:03:33.609 --> 00:03:38.293
"One time I saw a boy who was a rajah, an Indian prince.

60
00:03:39.614 --> 00:03:41.976
He spoke to his people just as you spoke to Martha.

61
00:03:43.237 --> 00:03:45.979
If they didn't instantly obey him, they would have been killed.

62
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.742
You are so different from Dickon."

63
00:03:49.983 --> 00:03:51.344
"Dickon? Who's that?"

64
00:03:53.212 --> 00:03:58.836
Mary told him all about Martha's brother and how he charmed the birds and animals with his music.

65
00:04:00.277 --> 00:04:03.079
"He knows about everything that grows or lives on the moor."

66
00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:06.721
"Oh, how can he like that dreary moor?"

67
00:04:08.062 --> 00:04:09.063
Mary protested.

68
00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:11.344
"It's the most beautiful place.

69
00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.967
I didn't like it at first, but now I do.

70
00:04:16.248 --> 00:04:18.089
You might even like it if you could go out."

71
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.131
"How could I go out on the moor?

72
00:04:21.511 --> 00:04:22.472
I'm going to die."

73
00:04:23.828 --> 00:04:25.389
"I don't like talking about dying.

74
00:04:26.629 --> 00:04:29.270
Let's talk about Dickon and then we'll look at your picture books."

75
00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.291
"There's one thing we haven't talked about—we're cousins!"

76
00:04:34.331 --> 00:04:38.752
For a few hours, the two children talked and laughed like ordinary ten year olds.

77
00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:46.995
Suddenly the door opened, and in walked Dr.

78
00:04:47.055 --> 00:04:48.155
Craven and Mrs.

79
00:04:48.235 --> 00:04:50.256
Medlock. Dr.

80
00:04:50.316 --> 00:04:51.376
Craven looked startled.

81
00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.761
"What's going on here?"

82
00:04:54.221 --> 00:04:54.762
he asked.

83
00:04:54.782 --> 00:04:58.605
"Oh, I don't know how this happened!"

84
00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:00.606
Mrs. Medlock was flustered.

85
00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:04.990
Colin explained how Mary had found him the night before.

86
00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:08.473
"And now we will have our tea here together."

87
00:05:10.294 --> 00:05:12.676
Dr. Craven did not look pleased at that news.

88
00:05:14.037 --> 00:05:16.499
But he didn't dare oppose his young patient.

89
00:05:16.519 --> 00:05:20.222
"I'm afraid you've had too much excitement today."

90
00:05:20.242 --> 00:05:23.780
"I'm better today," Colin said firmly.

91
00:05:24.401 --> 00:05:25.501
"Mary makes me better."

92
00:05:26.782 --> 00:05:28.122
Mrs. Medlock and Dr.

93
00:05:28.162 --> 00:05:32.524
Craven looked at each other in a troubled way, but there wasn't anything they could do.

94
00:05:34.345 --> 00:05:35.145
Still Dr.

95
00:05:35.185 --> 00:05:42.188
Craven was full of warnings for Colin: "Don't talk too much, don't forget you are ill, and don't

96
00:05:42.248 --> 00:05:43.548
forget you tire easily."

97
00:05:44.749 --> 00:05:46.290
Colin stared hard at Dr.

98
00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.671
Craven. "I want to forget those things.

99
00:05:51.011 --> 00:05:53.686
Mary makes me forget, and that's why I want her here."

100
00:05:54.991 --> 00:05:57.983
Dr. Craven looked very unhappy when he left the room.
